{
  "book": "helaman",
  "bookName": "Helaman",
  "chapter": 2,
  "voice": {
    "provider": "elevenlabs",
    "voice_id": "ddDFRErfhdc2asyySOG5",
    "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2",
    "settings": {
      "stability": 0.5,
      "similarity_boost": 0.75,
      "style": 0.35,
      "use_speaker_boost": true
    },
    "name": "Samuel"
  },
  "pauses": {
    "line_ms": 180,
    "verse_ms": 500
  },
  "duration": 226.278,
  "lines": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.619,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And it came to pass in the forty and second year of the reign of the judges,",
      "verse": "2:1",
      "lineIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 5.799,
      "end": 10.815,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "after Moronihah had established again peace between the Nephites and the Lamanites,",
      "verse": "2:1",
      "lineIndex": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 10.995,
      "end": 13.921,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "behold there was no one to fill the judgment-seat;",
      "verse": "2:1",
      "lineIndex": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 14.101,
      "end": 17.816,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "therefore there began to be a contention again among the people",
      "verse": "2:1",
      "lineIndex": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 17.996,
      "end": 20.829,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "concerning who should fill the judgment-seat.",
      "verse": "2:1",
      "lineIndex": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 21.509,
      "end": 30.333,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And it came to pass that Helaman, who was the son of Helaman, was appointed to fill the judgment-seat, by the voice of the people.",
      "verse": "2:2",
      "lineIndex": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 31.013,
      "end": 37.468,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "But behold, Kishkumen, who had murdered Pahoran, did lay wait to destroy Helaman also;",
      "verse": "2:3",
      "lineIndex": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 37.648,
      "end": 39.877,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and he was upheld by his band,",
      "verse": "2:3",
      "lineIndex": 8
    },
    {
      "start": 40.057,
      "end": 42.797,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "who had entered into a covenant",
      "verse": "2:3",
      "lineIndex": 9
    },
    {
      "start": 42.977,
      "end": 45.438,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that no one should know his wickedness.",
      "verse": "2:3",
      "lineIndex": 10
    },
    {
      "start": 46.118,
      "end": 56.288,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "For there was one Gadianton, who was exceedingly expert in many words, and also in his craft, to carry on the secret work of murder and of robbery;",
      "verse": "2:4",
      "lineIndex": 11
    },
    {
      "start": 56.468,
      "end": 59.719,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "therefore he became the leader of the band of Kishkumen.",
      "verse": "2:4",
      "lineIndex": 12
    },
    {
      "start": 60.399,
      "end": 63.51,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Therefore he did flatter them, and also Kishkumen,",
      "verse": "2:5",
      "lineIndex": 13
    },
    {
      "start": 63.69,
      "end": 66.569,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that if they would place him in the judgment-seat",
      "verse": "2:5",
      "lineIndex": 14
    },
    {
      "start": 66.749,
      "end": 74.04,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "he would grant unto those who belonged to his band that they should be placed in power and authority among the people;",
      "verse": "2:5",
      "lineIndex": 15
    },
    {
      "start": 74.22,
      "end": 77.192,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "therefore Kishkumen sought to destroy Helaman.",
      "verse": "2:5",
      "lineIndex": 16
    },
    {
      "start": 77.872,
      "end": 83.352,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And it came to pass as he went forth towards the judgment-seat to destroy Helaman,",
      "verse": "2:6",
      "lineIndex": 17
    },
    {
      "start": 83.532,
      "end": 87.712,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "behold one of the servants of Helaman, having been out by night,",
      "verse": "2:6",
      "lineIndex": 18
    },
    {
      "start": 87.892,
      "end": 92.536,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and having obtained, through disguise, a knowledge of those plans",
      "verse": "2:6",
      "lineIndex": 19
    },
    {
      "start": 92.716,
      "end": 96.06,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which had been laid by this band to destroy Helaman\u2014",
      "verse": "2:6",
      "lineIndex": 20
    },
    {
      "start": 96.74,
      "end": 99.434,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And it came to pass that he met Kishkumen,",
      "verse": "2:7",
      "lineIndex": 21
    },
    {
      "start": 99.614,
      "end": 101.843,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and he gave unto him a sign;",
      "verse": "2:7",
      "lineIndex": 22
    },
    {
      "start": 102.023,
      "end": 106.295,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "therefore Kishkumen made known unto him the object of his desire,",
      "verse": "2:7",
      "lineIndex": 23
    },
    {
      "start": 106.475,
      "end": 109.912,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "desiring that he would conduct him to the judgment-seat",
      "verse": "2:7",
      "lineIndex": 24
    },
    {
      "start": 110.092,
      "end": 111.95,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that he might murder Helaman.",
      "verse": "2:7",
      "lineIndex": 25
    },
    {
      "start": 112.63,
      "end": 117.228,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And when the servant of Helaman had known all the heart of Kishkumen,",
      "verse": "2:8",
      "lineIndex": 26
    },
    {
      "start": 117.408,
      "end": 119.869,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and how that it was his object to murder,",
      "verse": "2:8",
      "lineIndex": 27
    },
    {
      "start": 120.049,
      "end": 124.972,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and also that it was the object of all those who belonged to his band to murder,",
      "verse": "2:8",
      "lineIndex": 28
    },
    {
      "start": 125.152,
      "end": 126.313,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and to rob,",
      "verse": "2:8",
      "lineIndex": 29
    },
    {
      "start": 126.493,
      "end": 127.933,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and to gain power,",
      "verse": "2:8",
      "lineIndex": 30
    },
    {
      "start": 128.113,
      "end": 131.735,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "(and this was their secret plan, and their combination)",
      "verse": "2:8",
      "lineIndex": 31
    },
    {
      "start": 131.915,
      "end": 134.748,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "the servant of Helaman said unto Kishkumen:",
      "verse": "2:8",
      "lineIndex": 32
    },
    {
      "start": 134.928,
      "end": 137.389,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Let us go forth unto the judgment-seat.",
      "verse": "2:8",
      "lineIndex": 33
    },
    {
      "start": 138.069,
      "end": 140.623,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Now this did please Kishkumen exceedingly,",
      "verse": "2:9",
      "lineIndex": 35
    },
    {
      "start": 140.803,
      "end": 144.565,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "for he did suppose that he should accomplish his design;",
      "verse": "2:9",
      "lineIndex": 36
    },
    {
      "start": 144.745,
      "end": 147.113,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "but behold, the servant of Helaman,",
      "verse": "2:9",
      "lineIndex": 37
    },
    {
      "start": 147.293,
      "end": 150.358,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "as they were going forth unto the judgment-seat,",
      "verse": "2:9",
      "lineIndex": 38
    },
    {
      "start": 150.538,
      "end": 153.232,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "did stab Kishkumen even to the heart,",
      "verse": "2:9",
      "lineIndex": 39
    },
    {
      "start": 153.412,
      "end": 155.827,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that he fell dead without a groan.",
      "verse": "2:9",
      "lineIndex": 40
    },
    {
      "start": 156.007,
      "end": 160.001,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And he ran and told Helaman all the things which he had seen",
      "verse": "2:9",
      "lineIndex": 41
    },
    {
      "start": 160.181,
      "end": 161.388,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and heard,",
      "verse": "2:9",
      "lineIndex": 42
    },
    {
      "start": 161.568,
      "end": 162.59,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and done.",
      "verse": "2:9",
      "lineIndex": 43
    },
    {
      "start": 163.27,
      "end": 169.679,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And it came to pass that Helaman did send forth to take this band of robbers and secret murderers,",
      "verse": "2:10",
      "lineIndex": 44
    },
    {
      "start": 169.859,
      "end": 172.878,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that they might be executed according to the law.",
      "verse": "2:10",
      "lineIndex": 45
    },
    {
      "start": 173.558,
      "end": 178.248,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "But behold, when Gadianton had found that Kishkumen did not return",
      "verse": "2:11",
      "lineIndex": 46
    },
    {
      "start": 178.428,
      "end": 181.029,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "he feared lest that he should be destroyed;",
      "verse": "2:11",
      "lineIndex": 47
    },
    {
      "start": 181.209,
      "end": 184.228,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "therefore he caused that his band should follow him.",
      "verse": "2:11",
      "lineIndex": 48
    },
    {
      "start": 184.408,
      "end": 189.702,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And they took their flight out of the land, by a secret way, into the wilderness;",
      "verse": "2:11",
      "lineIndex": 49
    },
    {
      "start": 189.882,
      "end": 194.805,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and thus when Helaman sent forth to take them they could nowhere be found.",
      "verse": "2:11",
      "lineIndex": 50
    },
    {
      "start": 195.485,
      "end": 198.875,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And more of this Gadianton shall be spoken hereafter.",
      "verse": "2:12",
      "lineIndex": 51
    },
    {
      "start": 199.055,
      "end": 205.603,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And thus ended the forty and second year of the reign of the judges over the people of Nephi.",
      "verse": "2:12",
      "lineIndex": 52
    },
    {
      "start": 206.283,
      "end": 208.698,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And behold, in the end of this book",
      "verse": "2:13",
      "lineIndex": 53
    },
    {
      "start": 208.878,
      "end": 212.222,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "ye shall see that this Gadianton did prove the overthrow,",
      "verse": "2:13",
      "lineIndex": 54
    },
    {
      "start": 212.402,
      "end": 215.653,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "yea, almost the entire destruction of the people of Nephi.",
      "verse": "2:13",
      "lineIndex": 55
    },
    {
      "start": 216.333,
      "end": 219.444,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Behold I do not mean the end of the book of Helaman,",
      "verse": "2:14",
      "lineIndex": 56
    },
    {
      "start": 219.624,
      "end": 222.039,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "but I mean the end of the book of Nephi,",
      "verse": "2:14",
      "lineIndex": 57
    },
    {
      "start": 222.219,
      "end": 225.609,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "from which I have taken all the account which I have written.",
      "verse": "2:14",
      "lineIndex": 58
    }
  ]
}